{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","software--1","process--1","process--2","process--3","instance--d562b69c-9a04-5f30-a5ee-3888fe0b887b","instance--9439b417-d781-50b8-aca1-6c5c0147c0f4","software--4","software--5","process--4","software--6","instance--145c91f3-b41d-5b50-a2c8-50f9abebf50c","instance--b05ec101-c9e8-5f5f-9ccd-fe95076ad857","software--7","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--338a08d1-596c-5134-86e1-58bc27da7116","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--15a4f923-4743-5361-abc3-354a9eeed535","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--b3aa1b20-0a98-5bee-9b24-afe8c9468e2a","instance--c296e4bf-a60b-5aa7-afe4-a84efe3b46ee","instance--5ec67e94-f416-51dd-9822-ab000787efe6","instance--f64caa83-12dd-5204-a53f-519db6b69a9d","instance--f369065a-4305-5c0b-bf28-c38cb43b263d","instance--b9a6212e-3a83-51c0-a5dd-35899b0b0af4","instance--c14cdc44-61fd-5475-b158-40ad42c0c284","instance--958b80fd-829a-511c-b49f-68736d6d8cca","instance--132e46a7-c0ca-5199-8e75-7bdbb65da4fb","instance--b9dddad1-58ee-5919-ac4e-d08aed77b347","instance--dfb7a737-9df7-59df-be59-4c3b093cfccf","instance--aebcfa9f-8f3a-5d61-b94c-4adb89a08ea0","instance--e97a2eed-2ebb-5149-872b-ebf61e991ccf","instance--36b3f4bc-8e8a-54fd-8156-54d666e6c0e9","instance--dc65906c-5087-5f16-ab1e-0cc6b9d742de","instance--2b711834-bf74-52e7-9660-a150de46e6f8"],"properties":[["name","DEEP PANDA operations against national security think tanks"],["description","CrowdStrike described breaches at several national security think tanks involving webshell access, reconnaissance, PowerShell scheduled tasks, in-memory .NET payload execution, credential abuse, network share access, compression, and WMI-based lateral movement."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Dmitri Alperovitch"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","web.archive.org"],["url","https://web.archive.org/web/20200424075623/https:/www.crowdstrike.com/blog/deep-thought-chinese-targeting-national-security-think-tanks/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Maintain initial webshell access"],["description","For this same reason, DEEP PANDA likes to use webshells to keep low-footprint persistent access to the victim network, as we\u2019ve covered in our . This case was no exception, and that initial webshell implant allowed them to execute reconnaissance commands such as \u201ctasklist,\u201d \u201cnet view,\u201d and \u201cnet localgroup administrators,\u201d and then afterward to deploy the powershell scripts."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Run reconnaissance commands"],["description","This case was no exception, and that initial webshell implant allowed them to execute reconnaissance commands such as \u201ctasklist,\u201d \u201cnet view,\u201d and \u201cnet localgroup administrators,\u201d and then afterward to deploy the powershell scripts."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1087"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Deploy PowerShell scheduled tasks"],["description","Recently, we detected breaches of these networks via the use of powershell scripts deployed by the adversary as scheduled tasks on Windows machines. The scripts are passed to the powershell interpreter through the command line to avoid placement of extraneous files on the victim machine that could potentially trigger AV- or Indicator of Compromise (IOC)-based detection."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1053.005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Beacon to C2 every two hours"],["description","The scripts were scheduled to call back every two hours to the DEEP PANDA Command and Control (C2) infrastructure."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Download Wafer in memory"],["description","Once executed, it downloads and executes from memory a .NET executable (typically named Wafer), which in turn typically downloads and runs MadHatter .NET Remote Access Tool (RAT), one of the favorites of DEEP PANDA."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Run MadHatter from memory"],["description","Once executed, it downloads and executes from memory a .NET executable (typically named Wafer), which in turn typically downloads and runs MadHatter .NET Remote Access Tool (RAT), one of the favorites of DEEP PANDA. By running them from memory, it leaves no disk artifacts or host-based IOCs that can be identified in forensic analysis."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1620"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Mount network shares with stolen credentials"],["description","The adversary used stolen credentials to mount network shares via \u201cnet use\u201d command."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1021.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Bring in a tool"],["description","In one case, they brought in tool onto the system, but most of the time they leveraged existing Windows tools and avoided bringing many new tools into the environment that could make them noisy and easily detectable by technologies that scan for static IOCs."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Compress documents with 7-zip"],["description","After using compromised credentials to mount file shares, the adversary was seen compressing data using 7-zip. They were adding different document types to compressed files by wildcarding the extensions, such as:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1560.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Use WMI for remote deployment"],["description","For lateral movement, they used WMI to deploy the powershell scripts remotely and setup scheduled tasks on the remote systems."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1047"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:Fa